From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Kampert <DanielKampert@kampis-elektroecke.de>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] imx8mm: assign UART4 RDC domain to A53

By default the i.MX8MM RDC (Resource Domain Controller) config in
imx8mm_bl31_setup.c assigns UART4's master domain and peripheral
access permission to the Cortex-M4 (DID1), independent of whatever
the Linux devicetree says. Without this change, setting `&uart4 {
status = "okay"; }` in the kernel devicetree is not sufficient - the
A53/Linux side is blocked from the peripheral's registers at the
hardware RDC level regardless, since M4 firmware is never actually
used on this board and the M4-only lock just leaves UART4 unusable.

Reassigns both the master domain assignment and the UART4 peripheral
domain access permission (RDC_PDAP) from the M4 (D1R|D1W) to the A53
(D0R|D0W), matching NXP's own documented procedure:
https://community.nxp.com/t5/i-MX-Processors-Knowledge-Base/Enable-UART4-on-i-MX8M-Mini-A53/ta-p/1967129

Required for the Thread RCP (nRF5340) link on UART_4, see
meta-iot-gateway-os/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-toradex/iot-gateway-imx8mm.dts.
---
 plat/imx/imx8m/imx8mm/imx8mm_bl31_setup.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plat/imx/imx8m/imx8mm/imx8mm_bl31_setup.c b/plat/imx/imx8m/imx8mm/imx8mm_bl31_setup.c
--- a/plat/imx/imx8m/imx8mm/imx8mm_bl31_setup.c
+++ b/plat/imx/imx8m/imx8mm/imx8mm_bl31_setup.c
@@ -67,10 +67,10 @@
 #ifdef IMX_ANDROID_BUILD
 static const struct imx_rdc_cfg rdc[] = {
 	/* Master domain assignment */
-	RDC_MDAn(RDC_MDA_M4, DID1),
+	RDC_MDAn(RDC_MDA_A53, DID0),

 	/* peripherals domain permission */
-	RDC_PDAPn(RDC_PDAP_UART4, D1R | D1W),
+	RDC_PDAPn(RDC_PDAP_UART4, D0R | D0W),
 	RDC_PDAPn(RDC_PDAP_UART2, D0R | D0W),
 	RDC_PDAPn(RDC_PDAP_UART1, D0R | D0W),

@@ -114,10 +114,10 @@
 #else
 static const struct imx_rdc_cfg rdc[] = {
 	/* Master domain assignment */
-	RDC_MDAn(RDC_MDA_M4, DID1),
+	RDC_MDAn(RDC_MDA_A53, DID0),

 	/* peripherals domain permission */
-	RDC_PDAPn(RDC_PDAP_UART4, D1R | D1W),
+	RDC_PDAPn(RDC_PDAP_UART4, D0R | D0W),
 	RDC_PDAPn(RDC_PDAP_UART2, D0R | D0W),
 	RDC_PDAPn(RDC_PDAP_UART1, D0R | D0W),

